---
description: The plugin build and its traps
globs: ['packages/core/functions/**/*.ts']
alwaysApply: false
---

These fail silently. Check against the real toolchain before assuming.

- `@reference` suppresses `@utility` emission entirely.
- The compile must use `source(none)`, or a class name in a comment becomes a
  real utility in the shipped bundle.
- `addBase({'@utility …'})` and `addBase({'@theme': …})` emit verbatim and are
  never processed.
- A class written by JavaScript at runtime is never emitted through
  `addUtilities`. Route it through `addBase`.
- `matchUtilities` has no bare-value support; supply `values` explicitly.
- postcss-js camelCases properties and represents duplicates as arrays, which
  skip Tailwind's conversion back. Emit kebab-case, and preserve vendor prefixes
  (`-webkit-`, not `webkit-`).

Each build script cleans only what it produces. `dist/` belongs to `tsc`.
